          <p>False confidence here is an effective date, a calendar cutover, or a posted notice treated as if that effective instrument had created enforceable obligations or rights for the named parties, or a binding claim treated as proof the named effectiveness evidence was on the file. Evidence from the plant beats the effectiveness record when the record is being used as binding. Evidence from the plant beats the binding claim when the claim is being used as proof the named effectiveness was on the file. Evidence from the plant beats the note. A practice record that says effective is binding is not shown binding. Sync refuses to pretend effective or binding is a status light. Sync does not measure effectiveness. Sync does not measure binding. Sync does not measure effectiveness for the customer. Sync does not measure binding for the customer. Sync does not measure effectiveness or binding for the customer. Sync does not deem effective for the customer. Sync does not deem binding for the customer. Sync may surface an effectiveness record or a binding record beside Evidence, Verification, and the closed outcome. Surfacing is still a read. The closed outcome in that sentence is the Decision Case outcome record. It is not this effective, and it is not this binding. Sync must not auto-deem-effective or auto-deem-binding. Sync must not auto-deem-effective. Sync must not auto-deem-binding. Sync must not treat effective as binding as Learning credit. Recommend is not authorize. Direct plant execute stays off. CMMS write-back is not a live product path. Billing write-back is not a live product path.</p>

